ong thunderstorm near\nCanon City, or 32 miles west of Pueblo, moving south at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and nickel size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nFlorence, Canon City, and Penrose.","ends":"2026-08-20T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Canon City Vicinity/Eastern Fremont County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.be20d49feb7a54fb650261e09e298033196e1453.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.be20d49feb7a54fb650261e09e298033196e1453.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 20 at 3:07PM MDT until August 20 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Fremont County in central Colorado...\nNorthwestern Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 600 PM MDT.\n\n* At 307 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1.25 to 2 inches in 1\nhour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPenrose.","ends":"2026-08-20T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Fremont, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d32aeb759a775eed3c809ac03e0b5c34ac0a8e7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d32aeb759a775eed3c809ac03e0b5c34ac0a8e7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-